			title: "Gate to UXV"
			x: 42.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["54AF39C42293C4E7"]
			description: ["A shell of printed refractory high-entropy alloy that keeps its strength through heat and a field. It is the plain wall of the age: the Matrioshka Computer alone takes about 1,600, and the Mk5 ring about 1,350. The powder bed printer (400 ticks): 16 RHEA powders, 6 RHEA plates and 3 tungsten-fibre RHEA billets, for two casings. The body of nearly every UIV structure: the Pulser (about 1,050), the Penrose Engine (about 620), the BEUV Scanner (about 460), the Droplet Radiator Works (about 630) and the Pulsar Wind Trap (about 480). Powder, plates and billets by ME: you need thousands, so build it a dedicated line with several printers."]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "grindless:rhea_casing"
			id: "3071243DA1A3540D"
			rewards: [{ id: "1E0DEF931CEEBE33", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 64L, id: "14466CF158E7E9EC", item: "grindless:rhea_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "RHEA Casing"
			x: 26.5d
			y: 21.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3071243DA1A3540D"]
			description: ["A casing wound with metallic hydrogen cable that holds a field strong enough to confine a plasma or a star's matter. The reactor, the engine and the neutron machines are lined with it. The naquadria magnet works, circuit 12: 16 metallic hydrogen windings, 8 RHEA plates and 4 radiation-hardened controllers, for sixteen casings. The Penrose Engine (about 1,200), the Mk5 Fusion Reactor (about 1,000), the Pulsar Wind Trap (about 550), the Neutronium Compression Hall (about 540) and the Neutron Drip Works (about 420). The windings are the bottleneck; keep the Ramp Compression Pulser running and send them to the works by ME."]
			icon: "grindless:mh_field_casing"
			id: "5013B409A8F87BDE"
			rewards: [{ id: "5368D167D9264419", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 64L, id: "7EC9A5DAE5E32599", item: "grindless:mh_field_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Metallic Hydrogen Field Casing"
			x: 30.0d
			y: 21.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5013B409A8F87BDE"]
			description: ["A casing faced with lanthanum and boron carbide multilayers, which reflect extreme ultraviolet that every plain mirror absorbs. Machines that work with X-rays and 6.7 nm light are built from it. An assembler (400 ticks): 8 La/B4C multilayers, 8 RHEA plates, 4 glass interposers and a UIV sensor, with liquid nitrogen, for eight casings. The BEUV Scanner (about 740), the X-ray Pulse Profiler (about 515), the STM Lithography Cell (about 350) and the Positronium Condensate Lab (about 250). Multilayers and interposers by ME; liquid nitrogen by pipe."]
			icon: "grindless:multilayer_optics_casing"
			id: "1C8C0DC789C7FCD3"
