		{
			dependencies: ["1C8C0DC789C7FCD3"]
			description: ["A casing with a dilution refrigerator built in, cold enough that the spins of the matter inside stop moving. The labs that hold a condensate or a polarised source are cased in it. The nuclear demagnetisation stage, circuit 8: 8 mK cryostat modules, 8 RHEA plates and a UIV electric pump, with helium-3, for eight casings. The Positronium Condensate Lab (about 500), the Polarised Proton Source (about 215) and the Neutron Drip Works (about 130). Cryostat modules and helium-3 by ME and by pipe; the helium returns to the works."]
			icon: "grindless:dilution_cryostat_casing"
			id: "32A1DE0CD5EB4C17"
			rewards: [{ id: "171D29044494411E", type: "xp", xp: 140 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 32L, id: "5880C566129AF61B", item: "grindless:dilution_cryostat_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Dilution Cryostat Casing"
			x: 37.0d
			y: 21.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["32A1DE0CD5EB4C17"]
			description: ["The casing of the machines at the neutron star: osmiridium and reflector plate over radiation-hardened controllers, lined with polybenzimidazole. It is the one that does not leave the star. An assembler (600 ticks): 2 radiation-hardened controllers, 6 osmiridium plates, 2 neutron reflectors and polybenzimidazole, for eight casings. The Neutronium Compression Hall (about 840), the Neutron Drip Works (about 720), the Decay Heat Vault (about 490), the R-Process Decompressor (about 300) and the Crust Lift (about 250). Controllers and plates by ME; polybenzimidazole by pipe."]
			icon: "grindless:neutron_star_site_casing"
			id: "32DD9E9438EC0F6D"
			rewards: [{ id: "58AB7EDB38441560", type: "xp", xp: 140 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 64L, id: "5BB386880E6BDCD0", item: "grindless:neutron_star_site_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Neutron Star Site Casing"
			x: 40.5d
			y: 21.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3071243DA1A3540D", "72D797E3DDE7ED0E"]
			description: ["The first wall of the Mk5 ring: lithium-tin armoured tiles over a tungsten-fibre backing. It faces the plasma, and the divertor casing takes what is left of it. An assembler (300 ticks) makes four casings from 4 Li-Sn armoured tiles, 4 W fibre preforms and a UIV electric pump, with liquid Li-Sn. For two divertor casings, take one divertor and 2 Mk3 fusion casings. The Mk5 Fusion Reactor, which takes about 520 of them. The ring is too large for one pass of GTM's Terminal, which places about 2,300 per pass, so it takes two. Tiles and preforms by ME; the first-wall line is long, so make casings in a batch before you start the ring."]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "grindless:uiv_fusion_casing"
			id: "324F2FC31E9322CA"
			rewards: [{ id: "7A8C7F6CB965CEEB", type: "xp", xp: 160 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 64L, id: "377ABB5970B60753", item: "grindless:uiv_fusion_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "UIV Fusion Casing"
			x: 30.0d
			y: 23.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3071243DA1A3540D"]
			description: ["The part of the Matrioshka shell that sheds heat. Each module drops a curtain of tin droplets through free fall, and each one needs a pump to lift the tin back up. The assembly line (1,200 ticks, researched from the droplet collector): an orifice plate, 3 electron-beam distilled tin, a droplet collector, 2 UIV electric pumps and a UIV circuit. The Matrioshka Computer, which takes 22 of them. The shell is too large for one pass of GTM's Terminal, which places about 2,300 per pass, so it takes two. Pumps by ME, tin by pipe; ship modules down by ME from the orbit."]
			icon: "grindless:droplet_radiator_module"
			id: "57160B58FA826EA1"
			rewards: [{ id: "3DCAB0D52AEE6170", type: "xp", xp: 160 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ count: 22L, id: "5ABCA4ADE9671001", item: "grindless:droplet_radiator_module", type: "item" }]
			title: "Droplet Radiator Module"
			x: 33.5d
			y: 23.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5DFADD2C1B09AF2E"]
			description: [
				"The photonic chips of this age, then the parts, the circuit assembler and the hatches built from them."
				"The lithium niobate wafers come first."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:uiv_circuit_assembler"
			id: "32309B41A96F01BE"
