			title: "UIV Circuit Assembler"
			x: 22.5d
			y: 17.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["54AF39C42293C4E7"]
			description: ["The &6UIV Energy Hatch&r and &6UIV Dynamo Hatch&r are assembly line recipes on two UIV hulls, with metallic hydrogen cable, RHEA plates and FFKM seals. &6Metallic Hydrogen Single Cable&r carries the power. Two UIV machine hulls, three metallic hydrogen cables, six RHEA plates, six FFKM seals, three UIV circuits of any kind, three UIV sensors and a UIV motor. Every UIV machine that takes power from a hatch. Craft hatches and cable by ME in small batches; each machine takes one."]
			icon: "gtceu:uiv_energy_input_hatch"
			id: "3D4BC3A7590B186D"
			rewards: [{ id: "5F3A576C2576D7CD", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "18B7A3818E17CF51", item: "gtceu:uiv_energy_input_hatch", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5B0E9F3C7F3EE7FD", item: "gtceu:uiv_energy_output_hatch", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7CDFB1EB2153A1EA", item: "gtceu:metallic_hydrogen_single_cable", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "UIV Hatches and Cable"
			x: 25.0d
			y: 19.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["32309B41A96F01BE"]
			description: ["A thin film of lithium niobate on silicon makes the &6LNOI Wafer&r. The photonic foundry cuts it into thin-film modulators, and it is the base of the optical processor and of the nitride wafer next to it. An ion-implanted lithium niobate wafer, a silicon wafer and quicklime in the photonic foundry. The LN-on-Si3N4 wafer, the optical processors of the mainframe and the thin-film modulators of the tensor core. Implanted wafers by ME; one LNOI wafer gives many modulators, so stock modulators, not wafers."]
			icon: "grindless:lnoi_wafer"
			id: "1D71A54AB9C8A2EB"
			rewards: [{ id: "5B63C17F0B9709EF", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "5C757D3165C9C771", item: "grindless:lnoi_wafer", type: "item" }]
			title: "Lithium Niobate on Insulator"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1D71A54AB9C8A2EB"]
			description: ["The TFLN Fab slices an LNOI wafer onto a silicon nitride coated wafer and makes the &6LN-on-Si3N4 Wafer&r. It does not go into the mainframe: thinned and tipped with platinum it becomes the EO transceiver of the pulsar-timed repeater. The TFLN Fab, an LNOI wafer and a silicon nitride coated wafer. The EO transceiver of the pulsar-timed repeater and the UIV wireless hatches. LNOI wafers and nitride wafers by ME; the fab returns wafers to a chest."]
			icon: "grindless:ln_on_sin_wafer"
			id: "5F3FD5DD9FD7DBAA"
			rewards: [{ id: "3CA2E756FC79E223", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "71264424E4B1A667", item: "grindless:ln_on_sin_wafer", type: "item" }]
			title: "Lithium Niobate on Nitride"
			x: 9.5d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5F3FD5DD9FD7DBAA"]
			description: ["The TFLN Fab implants hydrogen into an isotopically pure silicon-28 wafer and slices off a thin film onto a handle wafer. The film is the &6Si-28 SOI Wafer&r that the quiet-qubit row needs; what remains is the &6Si-28 Donor Wafer&r. The TFLN Fab with a circuit of any UIV kind, and a silicon-28 wafer to slice. It draws UIV power. The silicon-28 SOI wafer of the later chapters. The donor wafer goes back to zone refining and is regrown, so no silicon-28 is lost. Feed handle wafers by ME and send the donors straight to the zone refiner; one loop keeps the isotope in circulation."]
			icon: "grindless:si28_donor_wafer"
			id: "11249E4704C3CD85"
			rewards: [{ id: "5A5FCAA1C17F4921", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "5C5ED279A8688B59", item: "grindless:si28_donor_wafer", type: "item" }]
			title: "Ion-Sliced Silicon-28"
			x: 12.0d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3B27271078AAEDC7"]
			description: ["A wafer exposed at 6.7 nanometres holds finer lines than any light before it: the &6BEUV-Exposed Wafer&r. The BEUV scanner (a UIV hull, UEV circuits), a tin-terbium droplet target, an HfO2 resist wafer and a BEUV mirror. The debris is caught and recycled. The BEUV driver ASIC next to it. Wafers by ME; send the fouled mirrors to the cleaning line, not to the bin."]
			icon: "grindless:beuv_exposed_wafer"
			id: "127106AB450BDD99"
			rewards: [{ id: "1EF0814AE2DDE468", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "30D318F8CE4D52FA", item: "grindless:beuv_exposed_wafer", type: "item" }]
			title: "BEUV Exposure"
			x: 7.5d
			y: 13.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["127106AB450BDD99"]
			description: ["Cut from the exposed wafer, the &6BEUV Driver ASIC&r is the logic that drives the photonic tensor core. A BEUV-exposed wafer, a VUV frequency comb and ethanol in the BEUV lithography line. The photonic tensor core. One wafer yields several chips; stock them in a chest by ME."]
			icon: "grindless:beuv_driver_asic"
			id: "1667D9ECE9C63D16"
			rewards: [{ id: "3344372EEA8AEA05", type: "xp", xp: 140 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "11C43C43F0D51D7D", item: "grindless:beuv_driver_asic", type: "item" }]
			title: "Driver ASIC"
			x: 11.5d
			y: 13.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1667D9ECE9C63D16", "1D71A54AB9C8A2EB"]
			description: ["Matrix products done in light: the &6Photonic Tensor Core&r is the arithmetic of the optical mainframe. It takes the compute module of the first pass of the hall. In the photonic integration hall (a circuit 4 program): a BEUV driver ASIC, a Photonic Compute Module and four thin-film LN modulators. The modulators come from the photonic foundry: an etched LNOI wafer and gold foil (circuit 6) make sixteen. The comb-fed tensor core, one pass later in the same hall. Modulators and ASICs by ME; the tensor core is made one at a time and goes straight to the next pass."]
			icon: "grindless:photonic_tensor_core"
			id: "3F6512C5FF0EBF55"
			rewards: [{ id: "56D249260071D23F", type: "xp", xp: 160 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "78ED46412EFC5732", item: "grindless:thin_film_ln_modulator", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7E682C6EF6E9D6BF", item: "grindless:photonic_tensor_core", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Photonic Tensor Core"
			x: 15.0d
			y: 13.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3B27271078AAEDC7"]
			description: ["A laser pulse a millionth of a millionth of a second long writes inside glass. The &65D Data Crystal&r keeps what it holds longer than the Sun will shine. A silica storage preform written by the femtosecond laser, engraved with a UHV circuit, then annealed in the electric blast furnace at 9,001 K. The Matrioshka research writes in Mercury orbit, the ergosphere probe bay and the Kerr probe. Silica preforms by ME; written crystals go to the research store."]
			icon: "grindless:data_crystal_5d"
			id: "5F6361D2A096AE06"
			rewards: [{ id: "10D504AFB6BB5530", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "73EA794520B79B4C", item: "grindless:data_crystal_5d", type: "item" }]
			title: "Five-Dimensional Crystal"
			x: 7.5d
			y: 16.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3B27271078AAEDC7"]
			description: ["The die has to be cold before it works. The &6mK Cryostat Module&r wets a rare-earth stage with a helium-3 mixture and holds the die at millikelvin. The nuclear demagnetisation stage: a nuclear stage, a cold plate and a helium-3/helium-4 mixture, with a circuit 2 program. The six-hour memory and the P:Si processor. The helium mixture returns to the works; send finished modules on by ME."]
			icon: "grindless:mk_cryostat_module"
			id: "741A4E00415BD039"
			rewards: [{ id: "115633C9C90A480F", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "5E6D3465F76B4438", item: "grindless:mk_cryostat_module", type: "item" }]
			title: "Millikelvin Cryostat Module"
			x: 7.5d
			y: 18.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["741A4E00415BD039"]
			description: ["A crystal of one europium isotope remembers a light pulse for hours when the right comb is burned in. That is the &6Six-Hour Quantum Memory&r. In an assembler: a hole-burned Eu-151:YSO slab (spectral hole burning with superfluid helium), an mK cryostat module, a UEV sensor and a circuit 20 program. The optical mainframe. Slabs by ME, helium by pipe; a few stocked memories are enough."]
			icon: "grindless:six_hour_memory"
			id: "53A536B775F9CA25"
			rewards: [{ id: "3DBE1A212FF60EE2", type: "xp", xp: 140 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "5224BA951F8FF24A", item: "grindless:six_hour_memory", type: "item" }]
			title: "Six-Hour Memory"
			x: 10.0d
			y: 16.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3B27271078AAEDC7"]
			description: ["A scanning tip peels hydrogen off silicon one atom at a time. The &6STM-Patterned Wafer&r is the silicon with the holes ready. The STM lithography cell: a hydrogen-terminated silicon wafer in ultra-high vacuum. The P:Si die, once phosphine fills the holes. Wafers by ME; the cell is slow, so run two."]
			icon: "grindless:stm_patterned_wafer"
			id: "32D6BBEFBFA91930"
			rewards: [{ id: "17AF2F6E34C9BFB3", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "155D7B8A6158F5CE", item: "grindless:stm_patterned_wafer", type: "item" }]
			title: "STM-Patterned Wafer"
			x: 7.5d
			y: 20.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["32D6BBEFBFA91930"]
			description: ["Phosphine fills the holes and silicon-28 grown over them seals them. The &6P:Si Die&r holds qubits made of single phosphorus atoms. The patterned wafer dosed with phosphine in the STM cell, then molecular beam epitaxy with silicon-28 and liquid nitrogen. Excess phosphine is scrubbed and kept. The P:Si processor. Phosphine by pipe in a contained loop; dies back by ME."]
			icon: "grindless:p_si_die"
			id: "5DB68611D99B3EB9"
			rewards: [{ id: "72A4D6369184985F", type: "xp", xp: 140 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "7F0A9CC9D347E680", item: "grindless:p_si_die", type: "item" }]
			title: "P:Si Die"
			x: 10.0d
			y: 20.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5DB68611D99B3EB9", "741A4E00415BD039"]
			description: ["A cooled die makes the &6Characterised P:Si Processor&r. It is the logic of the UIV circuit. The millikelvin cryostat works: a P:Si die, an mK cryostat module and liquid helium, with a circuit 3 program. The optical mainframe. Dies and modules in matched numbers by ME; keep one processor per mainframe."]
			icon: "grindless:p_si_processor"
			id: "5F5A39AD463A9E68"
			rewards: [{ id: "306A140944DC4CA9", type: "xp", xp: 200 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
